@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Registro correcto → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Dani@Test.com",
  "password": "supersecreta123",
  "name": "Dani"
}

### 2. Mismo email otra vez → 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dani@test.com",
  "password": "otracontraseña1"
}

### 3. Email mal y contraseña corta → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "esto-no-es-un-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Campo de más (intento de "mass assignment") → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hacker@test.com",
  "password": "supersecreta123",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 5. Login correcto → 200 + cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dani@test.com",
  "password": "supersecreta123"
}

### 6. Contraseña incorrecta → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dani@test.com",
  "password": "noesesta"
}

### 7. ¿Quién soy? (después del login 5) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 8. Cerrar sesión → 200 y borra la cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### 9. ¿Quién soy? (después del logout) → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 10. Mis tiendas → 200 con la lista
GET {{baseUrl}}/stores